1. MODULE AND PORTS

Every program begins with one module declaration, then declares all four ports exactly once:

module main;
port front: 4;
port back: 4;
port left: 4;
port right: 4;

Declarations must appear before executable statements. Names are case-sensitive.

2. STORAGE

Allocate byte-addressed CRAM or bit-addressed flip-flops (FF) before statements:

cram data: 16;
ff ready: 1;

CRAM sizes are bytes. FF sizes are bits, rounded up to bytes. Total CRAM plus FF bytes may not exceed 512. Storage names can be indexed, for example data[0].

7. COMPLETE EXAMPLE

module main;
port front: 4;
port back: 4;
port left: 4;
port right: 4;
let total = front ++ back;
front = total;
show(total.carry);

Compilation checks declarations and types. Keep every statement terminated with a semicolon.
